A||||4||Cutlass207TDC||Shaving my heads??||||5||
Z||000000||Cutlass207TDC||11-21-2001||02:11 PM||||If i get the heads on my 3.4 TDC shaved to up compression, how much of a power gain should i expect.  The compression is already at 9.5 to 1 stock.||||reg||5
Z||000001||cadaver||11-22-2001||06:32 PM||||You will need to run good gas with a higher ratio.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Galen||11-22-2001||09:51 PM||||If you use a nice wax, you can get a good shine on your head too <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||11-23-2001||12:53 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cutlass207TDC:<BR><B>If i get the heads on my 3.4 TDC shaved to up compression, how much of a power gain should i expect.  The compression is already at 9.5 to 1 stock.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Cutlass!<BR>Shaving the heads will not raise the CR enough to bother with...<BR>And if you shave too much, you will have to shave the intake, shorten the pushrods, and worry about leaks...<BR>Better to change the pistons for CR, but at 9.5:1, again, you are able to use regular gas, without worrying about detonation...<BR>Over 10:1 you need to run premium, and I would still add octane boost...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000004||lowCG||11-23-2001||12:22 PM||||Yep,not worth the time/hassle for the small increase in power.It'd be different if you were going from say,8;1,installing performance cams,but with the 10;1 that's already there;not much gain to be had.<BR>No pushrods,would only advance the cams slightly with the TDC motor.<BR>Do you have a good cold air intake already?<BR>If you're using a short exhaust,what are you doing for mixture tuning adjustments?||||reg||1
